1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,430
Every school has a ranking.

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:03,870
Nobody wrote it down.

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,070
Nobody voted on it.

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,564
And somehow… everybody knows it.

5
00:00:07,764 --> 00:00:08,914
This is Nia.

6
00:00:08,964 --> 00:00:10,194
It's her first day.

7
00:00:10,244 --> 00:00:11,794
And in about four seconds,

8
00:00:11,844 --> 00:00:15,573
this entire cafeteria is going to decide where she belongs.

9
00:00:15,853 --> 00:00:16,975
NIA: …hi?

10
00:00:17,375 --> 00:00:20,205
By Friday, one sentence in a group chat is

11
00:00:20,255 --> 00:00:22,525
going to rearrange this whole grade.

12
00:00:22,575 --> 00:00:25,565
So let's climb the seven levels of school popularity,

13
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:28,086
and find out who really decides them.

14
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:33,020
Level 1.

15
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:34,113
Invisible.

16
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:35,363
Nobody knows your name.

17
00:00:35,413 --> 00:00:36,883
Doors close in your face.

18
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:38,209
Teachers call you…

19
00:00:38,229 --> 00:00:38,695
MS. OKAFOR: Uh… you!

20
00:00:38,715 --> 00:00:39,745
In the hoodie.

21
00:00:39,945 --> 00:00:40,645
Good news:

22
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:42,295
you're not actually invisible.

23
00:00:42,345 --> 00:00:43,655
Everybody noticed you.

24
00:00:43,705 --> 00:00:45,578
They just haven't filed you yet.

25
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,090
Level 2.

26
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:48,370
The NPC.

27
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:50,450
People know your face, but not your name.

28
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,730
You're backpack kid.

29
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:54,290
You're the kid who sneezed during the assembly.

30
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:56,037
You are a side quest.

31
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:57,650
Level 3.

32
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:58,690
The funny one.

33
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,905
Theo can turn a pop quiz into a stand-up special.

34
00:01:01,925 --> 00:01:02,549
THEO: Pop quiz?

35
00:01:02,569 --> 00:01:04,158
More like… pop QUIT.

36
00:01:05,759 --> 00:01:07,069
It's not even a good joke.

37
00:01:07,119 --> 00:01:07,949
Doesn't matter.

38
00:01:07,999 --> 00:01:10,880
Laughter is currency, and Theo is rich.

39
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:12,260
Level 4.

40
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,910
The group chat admin.

41
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,830
Priya decides who gets added,

42
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:17,190
who gets left on read,

43
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:20,065
and which screenshot drops at 9 PM.

44
00:01:20,085 --> 00:01:20,668
PRIYA: Adding you.

45
00:01:20,688 --> 00:01:21,271
Adding you.

46
00:01:21,291 --> 00:01:22,194
Not you.

47
00:01:22,295 --> 00:01:24,005
She doesn't have the most friends.

48
00:01:24,055 --> 00:01:25,987
She has the most information.

49
00:01:26,590 --> 00:01:27,580
Level 5.

50
00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:28,700
The connector.

51
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,940
Marcus has a friend at every table.

52
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:32,060
Band kids.

53
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:32,730
Gamers.

54
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:33,980
The soccer team.

55
00:01:34,030 --> 00:01:35,580
If anything happens in this school,

56
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:37,245
it passes through Marcus.

57
00:01:37,265 --> 00:01:37,572
MARCUS: Yo!

58
00:01:37,592 --> 00:01:39,854
What's up, what's up, what's up!

59
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:41,740
Level 6.

60
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:43,420
Main character energy.

61
00:01:43,470 --> 00:01:45,820
Jordan walks down the hallway like a camera is

62
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:46,700
following him.

63
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:47,740
There isn't one.

64
00:01:47,790 --> 00:01:49,669
Okay… there is now.

65
00:01:49,769 --> 00:01:51,799
Everyone watches what Jordan wears,

66
00:01:51,849 --> 00:01:54,359
what Jordan says, and what Jordan likes.

67
00:01:54,409 --> 00:01:55,639
That's status.

68
00:01:55,689 --> 00:01:57,159
Not how much people like you,

69
00:01:57,209 --> 00:01:58,922
but how much they watch you.

70
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:00,430
And level 7?

71
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:01,310
It's locked.

72
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,190
Hold that thought.

73
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,639
We'll come back for it.

74
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:05,530
Here's the thing.

75
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:09,770
Psychologist Mitch Prinstein, who has studied popularity for decades,

76
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:12,008
says there are actually two kinds.

77
00:02:12,108 --> 00:02:12,808
Status:

78
00:02:12,828 --> 00:02:15,418
being seen, being powerful, being talked about.

79
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:16,858
And likeability:

80
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:19,178
people actually enjoying your company,

81
00:02:19,228 --> 00:02:22,371
trusting you, and feeling included when you're around.

82
00:02:22,571 --> 00:02:25,001
And the status ladder builds itself fast.

83
00:02:25,051 --> 00:02:26,921
In a classic summer camp study,

84
00:02:26,971 --> 00:02:30,441
a pecking order among 13-year-old boys was clear after

85
00:02:30,491 --> 00:02:31,721
just three days.

86
00:02:31,771 --> 00:02:32,761
Three days!

87
00:02:32,811 --> 00:02:35,564
That's faster than learning the Wi-Fi password.

88
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:37,220
Now.

89
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:37,940
Tuesday.

90
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,670
9:04 PM.

91
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:42,543
Somebody drops one sentence into the group chat.

92
00:02:42,843 --> 00:02:44,633
Jordan's new sneakers are fake.

93
00:02:44,683 --> 00:02:45,593
Is it true?

94
00:02:45,643 --> 00:02:46,713
Nobody checks.

95
00:02:46,763 --> 00:02:48,306
Nobody ever checks.

96
00:02:48,505 --> 00:02:50,455
One screenshot becomes ten.

97
00:02:50,505 --> 00:02:52,455
Ten becomes the whole grade.

98
00:02:52,505 --> 00:02:57,255
When researchers at MIT tracked about 126,000 stories on

99
00:02:57,305 --> 00:03:00,375
Twitter, false news spread farther and faster than the

100
00:03:00,425 --> 00:03:01,125
truth.

101
00:03:01,145 --> 00:03:02,695
Partly because it's new…

102
00:03:02,745 --> 00:03:04,549
and new is exciting.

103
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:06,150
Wednesday.

104
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:06,710
Lunch.

105
00:03:06,730 --> 00:03:08,075
Watch the tables.

106
00:03:09,975 --> 00:03:12,165
Jordan just went from level 6 to level 2.

107
00:03:12,215 --> 00:03:12,755
Overnight.

108
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:15,909
That's minus one thousand aura.

109
00:03:15,929 --> 00:03:17,077
DEV: Fake it till you make it,

110
00:03:17,127 --> 00:03:17,927
bro!

111
00:03:18,426 --> 00:03:20,056
And the kid who made the best joke about

112
00:03:20,106 --> 00:03:20,486
it?

113
00:03:20,506 --> 00:03:22,395
Level 5, by lunch.

114
00:03:22,695 --> 00:03:23,685
So who decided?

115
00:03:23,735 --> 00:03:24,965
Priya posted it.

116
00:03:25,015 --> 00:03:27,365
But Priya didn't move a single chair.

117
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:29,125
Every person who forwarded it,

118
00:03:29,175 --> 00:03:31,285
laughed at it, or stood up from that table

119
00:03:31,335 --> 00:03:32,245
cast a vote.

120
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,485
The ranking isn't a law of nature.

121
00:03:34,535 --> 00:03:35,685
It's an election.

122
00:03:35,735 --> 00:03:37,365
It happens every lunch.

123
00:03:37,415 --> 00:03:39,038
And everybody votes.

124
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,472
And then, a level 1 did something strange.

125
00:03:45,252 --> 00:03:47,336
NIA: Is this seat taken?

126
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,639
JORDAN: It's… literally all free.

127
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:51,059
That's it.

128
00:03:51,079 --> 00:03:52,069
That's the whole move.

129
00:03:52,119 --> 00:03:54,323
But Marcus, the connector, saw it.

130
00:03:54,523 --> 00:03:56,027
MARCUS: Scoot over.

131
00:03:56,427 --> 00:03:57,817
And when a connector moves,

132
00:03:57,867 --> 00:03:59,436
everybody notices.

133
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,990
This isn't just a nice story.

134
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:06,670
Researchers ran an experiment in 56 New Jersey middle

135
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,420
schools.

136
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:10,350
Small groups of students took a public stand against

137
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,092
drama and conflict.

138
00:04:12,192 --> 00:04:15,982
In those schools, disciplinary reports of conflict fell by

139
00:04:16,032 --> 00:04:17,582
about 30% in one year.

140
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:20,462
And the effect was strongest when the group included

141
00:04:20,512 --> 00:04:23,692
the students everybody pays attention to.

142
00:04:23,892 --> 00:04:26,482
The researchers called them social referents.

143
00:04:26,532 --> 00:04:28,482
You could call them level 5s.

144
00:04:28,532 --> 00:04:30,242
Turns out the people at the center of the

145
00:04:30,292 --> 00:04:32,482
network don't just spread rumors.

146
00:04:32,532 --> 00:04:34,219
They spread what's normal.

147
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:37,419
Which brings us back to level 7.

148
00:04:38,019 --> 00:04:40,929
Level 7 isn't the top of the status ladder.

149
00:04:40,979 --> 00:04:42,369
It's a different ladder.

150
00:04:42,419 --> 00:04:45,615
It's the person people are genuinely glad to see.

151
00:04:45,815 --> 00:04:48,885
Prinstein links chasing status to more anxiety,

152
00:04:48,935 --> 00:04:51,605
depression and relationship trouble later on,

153
00:04:51,655 --> 00:04:55,125
and likeability to better relationships and careers.

154
00:04:55,175 --> 00:04:58,085
One study even followed the cool kids of seventh

155
00:04:58,135 --> 00:04:59,685
grade into their twenties.

156
00:04:59,735 --> 00:05:04,227
By 22, their peers rated them as less socially competent.

157
00:05:04,427 --> 00:05:07,097
Status is how many people watch you walk in.

158
00:05:07,147 --> 00:05:10,217
Likeability is how many people are glad you did.

159
00:05:10,267 --> 00:05:13,303
Only one of those follows you after graduation.

160
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,650
So here's your side quest this week.

161
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,330
Don't forward one rumor.

162
00:05:18,380 --> 00:05:20,330
Learn the name of one level 1.

163
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,128
And once, just once, sit somewhere new.

164
00:05:23,528 --> 00:05:24,598
Which level were you?

165
00:05:24,648 --> 00:05:25,798
Tell us in the comments.

166
00:05:25,848 --> 00:05:27,412
We won't screenshot it.

167
00:05:27,812 --> 00:05:29,362
You're not just in the ranking.

168
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,122
You're one of the people deciding it.

169
00:05:31,172 --> 00:05:32,379
Make it ripple.
